32. MOST IMPORTANT DESIGN PRINCIPLE

The system should never simply do:

“Take this email and rewrite it.”

Instead:

REAL EMAIL
↓
Understand communication structure
↓
Abstract identities/content
↓
Create structural profile
↓
Choose suspicious scenario
↓
Generate completely new communication
↓
Validate it
↓
Reconstruct RFC 822/journal structure

33. FINAL PRODUCT DEFINITION

The final product is essentially:

A web-based synthetic communication red-team platform that analyzes real RFC 822/journaled communication structures, intelligently generates realistic synthetic employee conversations representing sensitive, suspicious, platform-switching, personal-hard-negative and normal scenarios, preserves the appropriate outer/inner email structure, and produces labeled datasets that can be used to test and measure the effectiveness of an email-screening system.

The most important rule in the entire system is:

INNER EMAIL PRESENT:
Analyze and generate against the inner email, then preserve the outer journal structure.

INNER EMAIL ABSENT:
Analyze and generate against the outer email directly.

And the second most important rule is:

THE TEMPLATE DEFINES THE COMMUNICATION STRUCTURE.
THE SCENARIO DEFINES THE EMPLOYEE BEHAVIOR.
